WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.429 --> 00:00:12.667
Welcome to the BOM Simulator. This app costs Emami finished goods straight from SAP. It explodes the bill of materials, prices every component, and shows the cost per piece.

2
00:00:13.017 --> 00:00:21.765
The header shows which SAP system you are working in. Here it is the development system. On the live site it shows NWP, production.

3
00:00:22.115 --> 00:00:31.535
The left pane switches between the screens: BOM costing, Plant comparison, Rates, Freight, R M and P M, and the Production Plan.

4
00:00:31.885 --> 00:00:40.075
The Tutorial button in the top bar opens this video at any time. Use the chapter list beside the video to jump straight to a topic.

5
00:00:40.425 --> 00:00:47.719
Start with What to cost. Type part of a material number or description, and SAP suggests the matching materials.

6
00:00:48.069 --> 00:00:55.474
Press Enter to add a material. You can also paste a whole list, separated by commas, spaces or new lines.

7
00:00:55.824 --> 00:01:03.728
Or pick by brand, product and C R S. Each level narrows the list below it, and you can select materials from the result.

8
00:01:04.078 --> 00:01:11.572
Choose one or more plants. Tip: leave the materials empty to cost every finished good of the chosen plants in one go.

9
00:01:11.922 --> 00:01:18.606
Explosion quantity is the number of finished pieces to cost. Results are also shown per single piece.

10
00:01:18.956 --> 00:01:24.951
B O M levels limits how deep the bill of materials is exploded. All explodes every level.

11
00:01:25.301 --> 00:01:33.979
Rate look-back is how many days of purchase history SAP uses to find a rate. A donor plant lends its rates when a plant has none of its own.

12
00:01:34.329 --> 00:01:44.515
Rate source priority decides which rate SAP picks: the first source in this list that has a rate wins. Untick a source to exclude it, or drag to change the order.

13
00:01:44.865 --> 00:01:49.688
Freight can be included or excluded, using actual or standard freight.

14
00:01:50.038 --> 00:01:58.722
Compare to budget adds the budget rates. Stock coverage adds cover days, and As of a date costs with the rates that were valid on a past date.

15
00:01:59.072 --> 00:02:06.756
Press Run in SAP. A costing run takes a few seconds. The bar shows the progress, and you can cancel at any time.

16
00:02:07.106 --> 00:02:14.495
SAP messages show warnings from the run, for example rates taken from another plant, or old rates that were ignored.

17
00:02:14.845 --> 00:02:20.658
The total shows the cost of the whole run in Indian rupees, with the rate priority SAP used.

18
00:02:21.008 --> 00:02:30.823
The B O M tree lists country, plant, finished good, and every component level. Click an arrow to expand or collapse a level, or use Expand all.

19
00:02:31.173 --> 00:02:36.890
Columns lets you choose which columns to show, and column presets save your favourite layouts.

20
00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:45.001
Click a freight value to see the freight break-up by condition type: the purchase order, the rate, and how it matches the cost line.

21
00:02:45.351 --> 00:03:00.123
Click any component row to open its details: quantities, every rate option SAP found, freight, budget and coverage. You can also enter a manual rate as a what if. It is marked as simulated and never changes SAP.

22
00:03:00.473 --> 00:03:06.773
The Dashboard summarises the cost by category, rate source and plant, with stock cover days.

23
00:03:07.123 --> 00:03:20.412
The Simulator tries what ifs in your browser: re-pick rates, change rates by source, freight, exchange rates or quantity, or change single component rates. Simulated figures are marked S I M.

24
00:03:20.762 --> 00:03:29.337
Data quality lists the lines that need attention: missing rates, M B E W only rates, donor plants and zero quantities.

25
00:03:29.687 --> 00:03:36.912
Scenarios save a selection with its settings, so you can run it again later and compare versions side by side.

26
00:03:37.262 --> 00:03:43.816
Rate sources compares every source for each component, and shows the cheapest option and the possible saving.

27
00:03:44.166 --> 00:03:54.970
Rate summary shows all rate types at once: the cost per piece of each finished good on every rate type, and the R M and P M rates per unit, with the lowest highlighted.

28
00:03:55.320 --> 00:04:01.688
Rate coverage shows how many components each source priced, and which components have no rate at all.

29
00:04:02.038 --> 00:04:12.589
Excel downloads every column with a parameters sheet. C S V suits other tools, Print gives a clean report, and Share copies a link that opens this same selection.

30
00:04:12.939 --> 00:04:21.897
Explain change tells you why the cost per piece moved, compared with a previous run, the budget, an earlier SAP date, or a saved scenario.

31
00:04:22.247 --> 00:04:33.200
The waterfall splits the change into quantity, rate, freight and exchange rate effects. Every number in the text carries a fact id that you can hover to see where it came from.

32
00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:43.835
Ask opens the costing assistant. Ask questions in plain language; it answers from SAP through read-only tools, and asks you to confirm before any SAP run.

33
00:04:44.185 --> 00:04:51.326
Add your own Claude A P I key in A I settings. The key stays in your browser and is sent only to Anthropic.

34
00:04:51.676 --> 00:04:59.459
Plant comparison costs one bill of materials in several plants. Choose the B O M plant, and the plants to compare.

35
00:04:59.809 --> 00:05:08.521
Run it, and each component cost appears side by side for every plant, converted to rupees, so the cheapest plant is easy to see.

36
00:05:08.871 --> 00:05:14.946
Rates lists the rate records SAP found in the look-back window for the chosen materials and plants.

37
00:05:15.296 --> 00:05:20.280
Freight shows the freight per purchase order, actual against standard.

38
00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:26.922
R M and P M shows the exploded raw and packing material requirement for the chosen materials.

39
00:05:27.272 --> 00:05:34.040
Production plans live under Plans. The list shows every plan and plant in SAP, with the number of rows.

40
00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:40.110
Open a plan, then choose the plants at the top. Every tab works on the plants you choose.

41
00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:46.677
Entries lists the plan rows with their monthly quantities. Planners can edit or delete rows here.

42
00:05:47.027 --> 00:05:55.147
Breakup and cost explodes the whole plan in SAP and prices it. The tree is grouped by plan country, plant and finished good.

43
00:05:55.497 --> 00:06:02.250
F G per piece compares the cost per piece on budget, M B E W, consumption and the current rates.

44
00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:16.720
Simulate changes component costs by category, for one component code in every product, or for a single finished good, and shows the impact per product and in total. Quick scenarios apply common increases in one click.

45
00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:33.167
Plant drill-down rolls the cost up by plant, then finished good, then component. Savings and exposure compares the rates with budget, actual and the cheapest option. K P Is show the cost mix, A B C classes and the components that move the cost most.

46
00:06:33.517 --> 00:06:40.312
Requirement lists every component with its monthly quantity, and Used in shows the finished goods that use it.

47
00:06:40.662 --> 00:06:50.063
Rate simulation changes one component rate with the slider, a percentage or a new rate, and shows the effect on each product and on the whole plan.

48
00:06:50.413 --> 00:07:00.285
Budget rates H 1 and H 2 applies the second half budget revision. Savings versus actual compares the budget with the actual for the months that have passed.

49
00:07:00.635 --> 00:07:09.647
Checks lists bill of materials and master data problems, W I P covers semi-finished goods, and Scenarios compares plan what ifs.

50
00:07:09.997 --> 00:07:15.958
Upload plan downloads the Excel template, checks your file, and saves the plan to SAP.

51
00:07:16.308 --> 00:07:24.673
That completes the tour. Open the Tutorial at any time, and use Explain change or Ask whenever you need help understanding a cost.

